{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>In wool or in linen.</b> Of wool or of linen — this is its plain sense. And its midrash: One might think he could bring clippings of wool and tow of flax and burn them with it? Scripture says ״הוּא״ — <b>it shall be burned in fire</b> — it does not need anything else with it. If so, what does Scripture teach by ״in the wool or in the linen״? To exclude the אֻמְרִיּוֹת in it, for they are of a different species; אֻמְרִיּוֹת is a term for edge-fiber, like אִימְרָא (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:21.164729011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}